  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The as-synthesized (MnNiSi)0.62(FeCoGe)0.38 alloy has high magnetocaloric and barocaloric performance.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The unchanged alloy has poor load-bearing integrity and is susceptible to cracking.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding approximately 2–5 at% Nb will refine the alloy's microstructure.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nb addition will stabilize grain boundaries in the alloy.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nb addition may promote ductile secondary phases.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Secondary-phase formation can improve load-bearing behavior.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6841954::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Nb-induced secondary phases will not disrupt the caloric transformation pathways.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nb atoms will slightly reduce the alloy's stacking-fault energy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduced stacking-fault energy can contribute to deformation modes associated with high toughness.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5321736::web::002::body"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nb-induced grain-boundary stabilization and altered local chemistry will suppress premature crack initiation and propagation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Minor Nb doping will improve ductility and fracture toughness.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Minor Nb doping will leave the thermoelastic caloric phase-transition mechanism largely unaltered.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Nb-doped alloy will show significantly fewer cracking incidents and better load-bearing properties than the unchanged alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The magnetocaloric and barocaloric responses of the Nb-doped alloy will remain within ±10% of those of the unchanged alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention is applicable under magnetic-field and pressure-field operation near the active caloric transformation temperature and under crack-inducing mechanical loads.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nb content must remain low enough to avoid changing the fundamental caloric phase transformation.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A controlled comparison of unchanged material and material containing approximately 3 at% Nb can test the proposed mechanical and caloric effects.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.design",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
